  "published": "2026-06-07T03:40:48.467Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.8: stable rollup of rc.1 + rc.2 + rc.4 — three additive bug fixes / diagnostics on top of 1.1.7, no breaking changes. (1) **Desktop OnBufferedAmountLow now actually fires.** SipSorcery has no native event hook; 1.1.7's DesktopRTCDataChannel declared the event but it was silent. 1.1.8 emulates the spec'd edge-triggered semantics via a 20ms-tick poller. Unblocks SCTP backpressure waits on desktop (was the silent reason 1MB+ tensor sends timed out at 30s in concurrent-await contexts even though buffer had drained). (2) **BrowserRTCPeerConnection connection-state polling fallback.** Chromium-under-Playwright fails to fire native `connectionstatechange` when the remote tab closes, leaving consumers (RtcPeer, P2PWebRtcBridge) stuck believing the peer is alive. 1.1.8 adds a 500ms-tick poll on `NativeConnection.ConnectionState`; when it differs from `_lastObservedConnectionState`, synthesises `OnConnectionStateChange`. Auto-stops on terminal state (\"failed\"/\"closed\"). Cancelled in Dispose. (3) **Opt-in `BrowserRTCPeerConnection.DiagnosticsEnabled` static flag** (default false). When true, the connection-state poller publishes per-tick state and synthesis events to JS globals (`__brrtc_pc_{N}`, `__brrtc_last_tick`, `__brrtc_synth_{N}`) for debugging. Off-default keeps zero JS-interop overhead in production. PMT 324/0/3 GREEN against this build.",
